        "text": "Summary\nThe Linux operating system is vulnerable to privilege escalation if it\u2019s poorly\nconfigured (or the kernel was not appropriately updated) by its root user. If\n272\nChapter 10 I Linux Privilege Escalation\nthat\u2019s the case, you have plenty of room to get a root shell. This topic is com-\nplex, and ideally you were able to understand it using the practical scenarios\nin this chapter and can use this knowledge in your own engagements. In the\nnext chapter, you will learn how to exploit the Windows operating systems.",
